timeline.body:
One more suggestion, and that will be probably my last :). What do you think about instead of checking if the name has multiple back references, we check if it has multiple matches?

Do you think that would work? Something like (not pretty but you can see what I mean):
```
               if (result.containsKey(key)) {
                    if (result.get(key) instanceof List<?> list) {
                        ((ArrayList<Object>) list).add(value);
                    } else {
                        List<Object> list = new ArrayList<>();
                        list.add(result.get(key));
                        list.add(value);
                        result.put(key, list);
                    }
                } else {
                    result.put(key, value);
                }
```
One of my concerns is that this could only work if the value is not of type list, but I think that is indeed the case. (btw, what I am trying to do is to not check this during the result but prepare the result on the right format upon creation).

What are your thoughts?

